{"agent_id":"pp3g-hHkP-review-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-9733","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:46:24.356274713Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2bcb7a02-f2b9-46d1-98d3-9b8dc2c757aa","comment_uuid":"88cc28e5-02a7-4587-a891-9f26a7c3791f","author":"pp3g-hHkP-review-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-9733","content":"Plan: INDEPENDENT review of #175 design. I will NOT read r1/r2 sub-issues (#176/#177). Steps: (1) verify fork/pin claims against live upstream (anomalyco/opencode redirect, tags v1.18.11/v1.18.12, provider.ts byte-identical, build script --single); (2) verify provider.ts patch against actual canonical source — check wrapSSE/wrapBody/AbortController wiring, signal composition, timeout:false interplay; (3) evaluate Option B vs relaxing guard for hy3 F2 preservation; (4) verify retry root-cause claims in source (retry.ts Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata unbounded, message-v2.ts fromError mapping, halt() path, RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS mechanism via Cause.done); (5) assess rebuild/replace/rollback safety (atomic mv, backup, autoupdate:false, wrapper REAL); (6) assess verification matrix sufficiency incl. slow-legit non-SSE and ctl.abort per-request. Verdict: PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL with findings. Post --kind result to #178.","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:46:24.349189729Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:DgzOYENynaMsZ7pCVxBifFWSjmnyiC8Jcxj9sNFn7oc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg0M4PxVoqjRN4Bb49LHWXhUMhFU3+sphEKDd9lwlE9xwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAKizavn3kosl9g2wjzYqvdZxOt4/OHl9IwmLH/+HS4dZ1lMwvG3gQTpCVGN5EvtTAqcHnG2Ai2qCo+BhitiqSCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:DgzOYENynaMsZ7pCVxBifFWSjmnyiC8Jcxj9sNFn7oc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg0M4PxVoqjRN4Bb49LHWXhUMhFU3+sphEKDd9lwlE9xwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKYImG/Dc798RvqhQXMqlzqiwcI6tdUNGgz3S6tPbGujHw6jeqcjZpbElmQSEiF5EHIK0kJL6Mpe1KiCEF0u1Qs=