{"agent_id":"pp3g-hHkP-review-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-9733","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:50:53.067376139Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2bcb7a02-f2b9-46d1-98d3-9b8dc2c757aa","comment_uuid":"d414af20-8aa3-4874-abf9-c472cd904fe1","author":"pp3g-hHkP-review-the-154-durable-opencode-silent-hang-fix-9733","content":"# REVIEWER VERDICT r3 (#178) — INDEPENDENT review of #175 design (durable opencode silent-hang fix)\n\n**Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS** — approve for implementation with 3 required fixes (R1 retry-budget off-by-one, R2 test-6 discrimination parameters, R3 test-7 concurrency spec). All load-bearing claims of the design were independently re-verified against canonical `anomalyco/opencode` v1.18.12 source and the live environment; no fatal flaw found.\n\nIndependent method: fetched and read `provider.ts` (2011 lines), `retry.ts`, `message-v2.ts`, `processor.ts`, `upgrade.ts`, `error.ts`, `script/build.ts` @ v1.18.12 (+ v1.18.11 provider.ts for byte-compare); verified the live wrapper, config, installed binary, and harness (`/tmp/opencode-hang-test/server.js`, `cfg/opencode.json`, `/tmp/opencode-145-patch/`). Did NOT read r1/r2 reviewer sub-issues (#176/#177).\n\n---\n\n## (1) Fork/pin strategy — PASS\n\n- **sst/opencode → anomalyco/opencode reconciliation: VERIFIED.** `curl -sI https://github.com/sst/opencode` → `HTTP/2 301` → `location: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode`; `gh api repos/sst/opencode` → `full_name: \"anomalyco/opencode\"`. Same repo, renamed; `anomalyco/opencode` is the canonical upstream.\n- **Tags/pin: VERIFIED.** Both `v1.18.11` (published 2026-08-01) and `v1.18.12` (2026-08-04) exist. `provider.ts` is **byte-identical** between tags (fetched both; `cmp` identical, 2011 lines). Pinning v1.18.12 (installed version) is correct; the one-line patch applies verbatim to either tag.\n- **Upgrade-survival: VERIFIED mechanically.** Wrapper `~/.local/bin/opencode` has `REAL=\"/home/claude-code/.nvm/.../bin/opencode\"` and runs `\"$REAL\" models` then `exec \"$REAL\" \"$@\"` — flipping REAL to the fork path works and the models-cache rewrite runs against the fork binary. `upgrade.ts:10` confirmed: `if (config.autoupdate === false || Flag.OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE) return`. Current global config has **no** `autoupdate` key (verified via json parse) — adding `\"autoupdate\": false` is additive.\n- **§0 current-state finding: VERIFIED.** Installed binary = 1.18.12 (mtime `2026-08-04 03:15:59`); `if(false)return` marker = **0 hits**; original guard string present (3 hits) — the #145 patch is indeed wiped and the bug is live. The urgency claim is accurate.\n\n## (2) provider.ts patch correctness — PASS with hardening notes\n\n- Hunk 2 target verified against the actual `resolveSDK` fetch wrapper (provider.ts:1737–1768): `customFetch`/`chunkTimeout`/`headerTimeout` extraction + `delete`, per-fetch closure, signals composition, `AbortSignal.any`, `timeout:false`. The design's dispatcher integrates cleanly: `bodyTimeout` extraction + `delete` mirrors the existing pattern; closure capture is correct; `?? DEFAULT_BODY_TIMEOUT` correctly preserves `false`/`0` disable semantics (`false ?? default` → `false`).\n- Hunk 1 `wrapBody`: mechanically sound and consistent with the **proven** wrapSSE pattern (#145 demonstrated abort+cancel+reject terminates a hanging body read). The direct `ctrl.error(err)` in the timer errors the wrapped stream even if `reader.cancel(err)`'s pending-read rejection is implementation-perturbed; per Streams spec, `reader.cancel` rejects pending reads, so the `catch` is belt-and-suspenders. New Response preserves headers/status/statusText.\n- Notes (non-blocking): **N2** `wrapBody` uses `start` + `for(;;)` with no backpressure → eagerly buffers the whole body (acceptable: non-SSE consumers use `text()`/`json()` anyway, but worth a comment); **N3** SSE + no `chunkTimeout` returns unwrapped even though `bodyTimeout` defaults on — optional hardening: fall back to `wrapBody` for SSE when `chunkAbortCtl` is absent, closing the \"any content-type\" gap fully (prod sets chunkTimeout, so not live-blocking); **N5** both timeout errors carry `metadata.code = \"ProviderResponseStreamError\"` (error.ts:16 `name`), so only the message (\"SSE read timed out\" / \"Body read timed out\") discriminates — fine for human logs, consider a distinct class/code if automated triage is wanted.\n\n## (3) Non-SSE deadline design (Option B) — PASS, semantically correct\n\n- Option B is the right choice. A **total-completion** deadline (single timer cleared only on `done`) precisely guards the actual failure mode (body never completes) and cannot false-fire on a slow-but-steady body — hy3 F2 preserved. Option A (per-chunk idle on all bodies) would false-abort any legitimate non-SSE body with an inter-chunk gap > chunkTimeout (5 min in prod) — a real, untested regression. SSE path is untouched (still `wrapSSE` + chunkTimeout).\n- `bodyTimeout` default 30 min < prod overall `timeout` 1 h → the body deadline fires **first** with a descriptive error. This matters because #144 proved the overall `AbortSignal.timeout` does NOT abort an already-resolved body read — bodyTimeout is the first effective bound for non-SSE. The explicit >30-min trade-off is documented and configurable; acceptable.\n- **R2 (required fix, verification side)** — §6.3 concrete slow-mode parameters contradict the matrix's own requirement. §6.2 row 6 says \"inter-chunk gaps > chunkTimeout\", but §6.3 specifies \"chunk every 2s for 6 chunks with chunkTimeout=3000\" — **2s < 3s**, so Option A would also pass; as parameterized, test 6 cannot detect a regression to guard-relaxation. Fix: gaps must exceed chunkTimeout (e.g., 5s gaps × 5 chunks = 25s total, chunkTimeout=3000, bodyTimeout=30000; also assert the same server minus completion aborts at bodyTimeout).\n\n## (4) Error surfacing + retry budget — root cause VERIFIED; REQUIRED FIX on predicate\n\n- Root-cause chain verified end-to-end in v1.18.12 source: wrapSSE abort → `ProviderError.ResponseStreamError` → `MessageV2.fromError` case at message-v2.ts:665 → `APIError{isRetryable:true}` → `retryable()` returns a retry payload (retry.ts:71–75, 122) → `SessionRetry.policy()` = `Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata` with **no recurs cap** (retry.ts:176–199) → `Effect.retry(...)` in processor.ts:660–674 → infinite silent retry, zero ERROR. `halt()` (processor.ts:599–625) does `Effect.logError` + `Session.Event.Error` + `assistantMessage.error` + status idle, but is reachable only when the schedule gives up. Design's diagnosis is exact.\n- Cap mechanism (`Cause.done`) is mechanically correct — identical to the existing non-retryable stop path (`if (!retry) return Cause.done(meta.attempt)`, retry.ts:185).\n- **R1 (required fix) — off-by-one in the retry-budget predicate.** `meta.attempt` is a **1-based RETRY count**, not total attempts: verified via `delay(attempt)` = `RETRY_INITIAL_DELAY × 2^(attempt-1)` (retry.ts:65) — attempt=1 → 2000ms, matching the observed first-retry gap in #145. Therefore `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3` with stop at `meta.attempt > RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` yields **3 retries + initial = 4 total POSTs**, contradicting the design's own \"3 attempts total\" (§4.2.2) and \"≤3 POSTs\" (§6.4). Specify precisely: either `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` = **total attempts** with stop at `meta.attempt >= RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (2 retries → 3 total), or rename to `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES = 2` with `meta.attempt > RETRY_MAX_RETRIES`. The §6.4 assertion \"exactly ≤3 POSTs\" then holds.\n- Note: the cap bounds attempt COUNT, not total DELAY (retry-after headers can still produce multi-minute waits) — acceptable for the hang case (no retry-after headers) and keep explicit. **N4:** test 1's \"process exits with error, not EXIT 124\" is an unverified assumption about `opencode run` exit behavior — the load-bearing assertions are the visible ERROR entry + `Session.Event.Error` + ≤3 POSTs.\n\n## (5) Rebuild/replace/rollback — PASS with one note\n\n- `build.ts:19`/116–122: `--single` filters targets to current platform; outfile `dist/<name>/bin/opencode` — VERIFIED. Bun-not-installed prereq is accurately stated.\n- Backup (.stock-1.18.12), `.previous` rotation, and rollback (restore binary or flip REAL back) are concrete, reversible, and operate on the npm-independent path — the upgrade-wipe vector is genuinely closed.\n- **N1:** §5.2 places the fork binary with `cp` despite the \"atomic\" heading. `cp` is not atomic; a truncated copy could break a concurrent launch through the wrapper. Use a same-filesystem `mv` (build output → temp → `mv` into `~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/`), matching the #145 procedure that was already proven (\"Installed via atomic mv\").\n\n## (6) Verification harness — CONDITIONAL (R2, R3)\n\n- Reuse claims verified: server.js `HANG_MODE` 0/1/2 semantics exactly as described (0 = no response → headerTimeout; 1 = headers then hang → chunk/body deadline; 2 = one SSE chunk then hang); cfg has chunkTimeout/headerTimeout/timeout and can gain bodyTimeout; artifacts (`/tmp/opencode-145-patch/`) intact.\n- **R2** — see §3: slow-mode parameters must discriminate Option B from Option A (gaps > chunkTimeout).\n- **R3** — test 7 (ctl.abort per-request) is underspecified: current server.js applies ONE mode to ALL requests, so \"two concurrent requests\" cannot be exercised without a per-request-differentiating mode (e.g., request #1 hangs, request #2 healthy). Note: source inspection already answers hy3 F4 — provider.ts:1746 creates `new AbortController()` **inside** the per-request fetch closure, so the abort controller is per-request, not shared. Test 7 may be implemented as a documented confirmation; if the concurrency server mode is added, do it as spec'd above.\n- Matrix otherwise sufficient: json + SSE hang modes, healthy controls (tests 4/5), sensitivity test 8, and the ≤3-POST retry-budget assertion (§6.4) which becomes load-bearing once R1 is fixed.\n\n---\n\n## Required fixes before/at implementation\n\n- **R1** — Pin retry-budget semantics: `meta.attempt` is 1-based retry count; make \"3 attempts total (initial + 2 retries)\" ↔ §6.4 \"≤3 POSTs\" ↔ predicate (`meta.attempt >= RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` with constant=total, or rename to RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2) consistent.\n- **R2** — Test 6 slow-non-SSE mode: inter-chunk gaps MUST exceed chunkTimeout (e.g., 5s gaps, chunkTimeout=3000, total < bodyTimeout=30000) so only Option B passes; add the never-completes variant asserting abort at bodyTimeout.\n- **R3** — Test 7: add a per-request-differentiating server mode (first hangs, second healthy) or explicitly downgrade to source-confirmed F4 verification (provider.ts:1746).\n\n## Minor notes (non-blocking)\n\nN1 atomic `mv` (not `cp`) for the fork-binary install; N2 wrapBody eager buffering — add a comment; N3 optional SSE fallback to wrapBody when chunkTimeout absent; N4 verify `opencode run` exit-code on session error during implementation; N5 consider distinct error metadata beyond message for the two timeout paths.\n\n**Bottom line**: the design is accurate, evidence-backed, and its mechanisms are verified against canonical source. With R1–R3 addressed, it fully satisfies #154's four requirements (source rebuild + upgrade survival, distinct non-SSE deadline preserving hy3 F2, error surfacing + retry budget killing the silent infinite retry loop, and verification incl. slow-legit non-SSE + per-request abort).","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:50:53.060094546Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:DgzOYENynaMsZ7pCVxBifFWSjmnyiC8Jcxj9sNFn7oc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg0M4PxVoqjRN4Bb49LHWXhUMhFU3+sphEKDd9lwlE9xwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAQVI1Ensl18h6yMsnmvJXWTmGaadRI4sxwtqbE1q+JA9HzBiGRkVQkSjkzh5aWQbPHLX8xVcqA4AfH9EBtXjUAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:DgzOYENynaMsZ7pCVxBifFWSjmnyiC8Jcxj9sNFn7oc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg0M4PxVoqjRN4Bb49LHWXhUMhFU3+sphEKDd9lwlE9xwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCrH5QRir3gzLkZ0Fmrk55o6x/wA7nMRdBVPDGem251fevTutEpzweR/RPhhcj3n3GncCciOLbdiqjf+7LMV/Qs="}
